# pizero-platform

The Waveshare PiZero family: an RP2 chip on a board in the Raspberry Pi Zero's
outline, with its 40-pin header, a DVI connector, a TF card socket, and two
USB-C sockets, the native port and a PIO-USB port. rp2350_pizero is the
RP2350-PiZero, and rp2350_pizero_usb_host the same board with its PIO-USB port
a USB host.

rp2350_pizero binds platform.pizero.sdcard, its TF socket in 4-bit SD mode
through mm.sdcard's SdioCard, as mm.sdcard.socket; modules/mm has no DVI output
yet. rp2350_pizero_usb_host
inherits the socket and binds platform.pico.usb.host to the PIO-USB port.
